 "result_text": "`checkout_github_prs()` now warns and returns, instead of raising, when no PRs match the criteria. I haven't run the tests or tried it against a real repository.\n\nThe change is in `git_machete/client.py`:\n- **Warnings instead of errors:** `__get_valid_pull_requests` warns instead of raising for four cases:\n  - none of the given PR numbers are found;\n  - `--all` finds no open PRs;\n  - `--mine` finds no open PRs for the current user;\n  - `--by` finds no open PRs for that user.\n- **Early return:** `checkout_github_prs` now returns right after that lookup when there are no PRs. So it no longer fetches the remote or touches the definition file.\n\nI left one case as an error: asking for a single PR number that doesn't exist still raises `MacheteException`. I read that as a bad explicit argument rather than \"no PRs for the criteria\". If you'd rather have that one warn too, it's a one-line change.\n\nIf existing tests assert the old exception messages for these cases, they'll need updating. I didn't touch any tests.",
